# Environment Variables

Copy this file to `.env.local` for local development.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Owner Auth (Netlify Function — server-side only)
# These MUST NOT be prefixed with VITE_ — they are never exposed to the browser.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────

# Password for the owner-only mode on the Resume AI page
OWNER_PASSWORD=your_password_here

# Gemini API key (optional — owner can use Gemini if this is set)
# Get one free at: https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
GEMINI_API_KEY=AIzaSy...

# OpenRouter API key (optional — owner can use OpenRouter if this is set)
# Get one at: https://openrouter.ai/keys
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-...

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Notes
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# - At least one of GEMINI_API_KEY or OPENROUTER_API_KEY must be set for owner mode.
# - If both are set, OpenRouter is used as the default provider.
# - These variables are only available inside `netlify/functions/auth.ts`.
# - Public users bring their own keys — nothing is stored on the server for them.
# - For local development with the Netlify Function: run `bunx netlify dev` instead
#   of `bun run dev`. Public mode works fine with just `bun run dev`.
